> 
> Hello Peyton,
> I truly enjoyed our conversation and wanted to explore whether there may still be opportunity to support your work, I believe I have a lot to offer to this role, and with the understanding that you’re prioritizing candidates with a strong background in high-net-worth individual (HNWI) fundraising. I’d like to take a moment to highlight some examples from my experience that demonstrate my capabilities in this area:
> At the Institute for Market Transformation, I successfully established an individual giving stewardship strategy and raised over $50,000 in new gifts within twelve months, including the following key milestones:
> 100% board participation in giving for the first time since IMTs inception.
> Stewarded a new donor, friend of board member, to give $10K which was a significant personal gift for him and IMT.
> Piloting a new advisory board, which directly involved high-net-worth individuals invested in building innovation in the DC metro area
> 
> Previously, Clean Energy Buyers Association, I was the top salesperson at the company, and brought in over 70 blue chip members companies including Patagonia, Airbnb, Mastercard, Marriott with a total membership revenue of $800K and raised over $80K in event sponsorship within twenty-four months.
> My role was focused on corporate relationships, however, I have consistently built and sustained relationships with the decision makers, many of whom are high-net-worth individuals or representatives of significant corporate assets. These engagements included facilitating deals and securing memberships that required a keen understanding of donor motivations and strategic interests.
> 
> With The Climate Group in New York and London, I curated our annual HNW events and award ceremonies at private homes through tailored engagement and bespoke communication strategies, fostering personal relationships with high level donors, many of whom FZS-US will also want to court including members of the B-Team.
>  
> I believe these experiences underscore my ability to connect with, engage, and maximize contributions from high-net-worth individuals to further your mission effectively. My personality and ability to move confidently within American and European contexts will also allow me the comfort to navigate both markets.
> 
> Outside of work, I had led a successful matchmaking business, focused on elite clients.  Many of the relationship building tools are applicable to fundraising work and I would be happy to share success stories from this arena as well.
>  
> Perhaps I can come down to DC later in April to connect with you in person, I would be delighted to continue the conversation and add more detail to the 90 day strategy I shared in my previous email, reframing with a focus that will set us up for short and long term wins with new HNWIs. 
>  
> Thank you,
> Johanna
