> to Christof, Marianne, Peyton
> 
> 
> 
> 
> Dear Christof and Marianne, 
> 
> 
> Thank you very much for your time, it was a pleasure meeting with you virtually. I wanted to provide more detail on the strategy I described for finding more HNWIs in the US to grow our impact, where I would begin my 90 days if selected for this role.
> 
> 
> The basis for the appeal to our largest audience is that "this is the moment because tomorrow is too late"—We must embrace a sense of urgency because we sincerely do not know what is going to happen tomorrow. So, creating a unique moment—a connection, a human-to-human interaction with an animal or a piece of land, rather than a mass email—is a special, perhaps ephemeral connection is something I will try to foster with each new person (prospective donor), because otherwise, why are we trying to do this work at all? I sincerely believe it's about connecting to, and feeling a part of something bigger. 
> 
> 
> Outline for Action:
> Action 1: Articulate our value proposition, what sets us apart and why NHWI should give now ("urgency") 
> Activity: Conversation across teams (internal to our org) and with existing donors about the value they see in our work. 
> Action 2: Take inventory of who is already in our network (SalesFroce deepdive) then map how each group is served and identify areas for improvement. 
> Activity: Updating our records and assigning clear relationship managers, plus additional bespoke services ("upselling accounts"). 
> Thank you campaigns across all gift levels. 
> Strategy: Encourage current board members to introduce us to prospective donors within their networks. This includes appointing a board chair and setting fundraising expectations for all participants.
> Build the board and uninterrupted cyles of funding--identify new onramps for supporters (Wealth-X or Forbes) and new locations for leads. 
> Action 3: Engagement Through Events
> Activity:  Host events, partner with aligned organizations, and use social media/newsletters to share compelling stories, emphasizing transparency and accountability in how funds are used.
> Strategy: Communications Revamp: Update and tailor our messaging to match the moment.
> Be open to a different format (taking it into or out of the digital age): 
> Goal: We want those who engage with us to get a "unique and authentic experience --to touch and see something that may not otherwise exist, cherished and sustainably protected for their intrinsic and economic value to present and future generations." 
> Thank you for your time and consideration, 
> Johanna
