> 
> Hello Peyton,
> 
> I greatly enjoyed our conversation and wanted to discuss potential opportunities to support your mission. I have strong expertise in high-net-worth individual (HNWI) fundraising and believe I can significantly contribute to this role. Here are a few highlights from my background:
> 
> 1. **Institute for Market Transformation:** I created a donor stewardship strategy that raised over **$50,000** in a year, achieving 100% board participation in giving and securing a **$10K** gift from a new donor. I also spearheaded a new advisory board that engaged HNWIs focused on innovation in the DC metro area.
> 
> 2. **Clean Energy Buyers Association:** As the top salesperson, I onboarded **70+ blue-chip companies**, including Patagonia and Airbnb, generating **$800K** in membership revenue and **$80K** in event sponsorships within two years. I excelled at building enduring relationships with decision-makers, including many HNWIs.
> 
> 3. **The Climate Group:** In both NYC and London, I curated HNW events and award ceremonies, employing tailored engagement strategies to foster strong relationships with top donors, many of whom are key targets for FZS-US.
> 
> These experiences demonstrate my ability to effectively connect with and engage HNWIs to advance your organization's mission. I am comfortable navigating both American and European markets, further enhancing my potential contributions.
> 
> Additionally, my previous leadership of a successful matchmaking business for elite clients equips me with unique relationship-building skills applicable to fundraising. I'm excited to share success stories from that experience as well.
> 
> I'd love to visit DC later this month to discuss this in person and delve deeper into the **90-day strategy** I shared previously. Together, we can frame it to ensure both short- and long-term success with new HNWIs.
> 
> Thank you for considering my application. I look forward to the opportunity to contribute to your mission.
> 
> Best regards,
> 
> Johanna Goetzel  
